        <helo1:HELO_9000007 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000007 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_4000003"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000007 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_4000005"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000001"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000008"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.50</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">2 of the 4 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Select unit costs are core concepts of Counting the Cost (Cost Valuation, Micro-Costing), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000001"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000020"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.50</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">1 of the 2 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Value resource use are core concepts of Counting the Cost (Cost Valuation), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. This proposal rests on a single concept, so it is weaker. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000001"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000007"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_4000001"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">Review B of HELO 0.2.0 (19 October 2026) proposes that Counting the Cost is primarily for the student, for Darrin Baines to confirm. The site does not state who the pathway is for.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000020>primarily</helo1:HELO_9000020>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000001"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000007"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_4000002"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">Review B of HELO 0.2.0 (19 October 2026) proposes that Counting the Cost is primarily for the health economist, for Darrin Baines to confirm. The site does not state who the pathway is for. The HETO route, through the practitioner roles of the tasks the pathway is proposed to prepare for, gives the same profile.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000020>primarily</helo1:HELO_9000020>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000001"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000007"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_4000003"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">Review B of HELO 0.2.0 (19 October 2026) proposes that Counting the Cost is also for the health technology assessment analyst, for Darrin Baines to confirm. The site does not state who the pathway is for.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000020>also</helo1:HELO_9000020>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000001"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000007"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_4000005"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">Review B of HELO 0.2.0 (19 October 2026) proposes that Counting the Cost is also for the economic modeller, for Darrin Baines to confirm. The site does not state who the pathway is for.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000020>also</helo1:HELO_9000020>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000002 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000002">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_0000001"/>
        <helo1:HELO_1000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_6000004"/>
