    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000003"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000001"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.67</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">2 of the 3 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Conduct a model-based economic evaluation are core concepts of Judging Value for Money (Cost-Effectiveness Analysis, Economic Evaluation), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000003"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000004"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1.00</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">The one HEO concept that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Set the time horizon (Time Horizon) is a core concept of Judging Value for Money, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. This proposal rests on a single concept, so it is weaker. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000003"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000010"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.67</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">2 of the 3 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Add discounting to an economic model are core concepts of Judging Value for Money (Discount Rate, Present Value), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000003"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000012"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.57</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">4 of the 7 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Calculate incremental cost-effectiveness results are core concepts of Judging Value for Money (Cost-Effectiveness Threshold, Dominance, Extended Dominance, Incremental Cost-Effectiveness Ratio (ICER)), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000003"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000016"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.50</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">1 of the 2 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Report an economic evaluation are core concepts of Judging Value for Money (Economic Evaluation), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. This proposal rests on a single concept, so it is weaker. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
