        <helo1:HELO_9000007 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000007 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_4000003"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000007 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_4000005"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000005"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000005"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1.00</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">2 of the 2 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Develop an economic model are core concepts of Building the Model (Health Economic Model, Parameter Estimation), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000005"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000006"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.60</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">3 of the 5 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Conceptualise the model structure are core concepts of Building the Model (Decision Tree, State Transition Model, Structural Uncertainty), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000005"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000013"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1.00</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">4 of the 4 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Conduct sensitivity analysis are core concepts of Building the Model (Parameter Uncertainty, Scenario Analysis, Sensitivity Analysis, Structural Uncertainty), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000005"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000014"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1.00</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">3 of the 3 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Run a deterministic sensitivity analysis are core concepts of Building the Model (Deterministic Sensitivity Analysis, One-Way Sensitivity Analysis, Tornado Diagram), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_5000005"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_9000006"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_4000015"/>
        <ns1:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <ns2:HEAO_9000001 rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heao/HEAO_4000002"/>
        <helo1:HELO_9000009 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.50</helo1:HELO_9000009>
        <helo1:HELO_9000010 xml:lang="en">3 of the 6 HEO concepts that HETO 0.3.0 relates to the task Run a probabilistic sensitivity analysis are core concepts of Building the Model (Monte Carlo Simulation, Parameter Distribution, Probabilistic Sensitivity Analysis), at least half, so the build proposes that the pathway prepares for the task. HETO&apos;s own relationships from tasks to HEO concepts are proposals too. The pathway builds understanding of these concepts and does not train the task. Representational is the nearest of the five linking kinds of HEAO 0.2.0. Preparing a learner for a task is none of them exactly.</helo1:HELO_9000010>
        <helo1:HELO_9000021 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</helo1:HELO_9000021>
        <helo1:HELO_9000022 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</helo1:HELO_9000022>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
